title the crashed meteor -- the status bumps, the seed takes its living name, and the wall catches its own publisher
prompt Keaton: bump the root README status from primordial to crashed-meteor, and the seed's force-push single commit becomes grain-ww instead of Grain OS, crashed meteor instead of initial public seed.
think The bump swept the front door whole rather than one badge: README's status badge reads crashed-meteor, CHANGELOG and SECURITY's phase sentences follow (both ship in the seed), the comlink-tendency rule's phase clause follows, and the corpora mirrors were written by the mirror tool rather than by hand. The stamp-named foundation keeps its primordial word -- testimony by the mark law's own basename test.
think The identity rename rode through every layer that speaks it, proven at each: publish-seed.sh commits as grain-ww <grain-ww@users.noreply.github.com> with subject grain-ww -- the crashed meteor; the commit-msg hook's seed exemption prefix moved from Grain OS -- to grain-ww -- (one live prefix, the elder living only in force-discarded seed history); the guard scan's welcome case follows; and both git-signing twins plus the mechanism-sentence rule carry the rename with its date and reason -- the name now matches the living domain grain-ww.com.
obs The republish refused on its first run, and the refusal was the wall catching its own publisher. Tonight's earlier publish had written core.sshCommand -- whose path carries the host USERNAME -- into seed/.git/config, and the leak scan read it: IDENT_LEAK, seed/.git/config. The config never ships to GitHub, and the wall is right anyway -- nothing identity-bearing belongs anywhere under seed/. Two corrections, both in the publisher: the transport became a GIT_SSH_COMMAND environment variable that arms one push and touches no disk, and the .git wipe moved BEFORE the witness, so the scan reads exactly the bytes that ship and nothing beside them.
obs Shipped and verified: grain-os/grain forced c06eb0a -> e507f1c, one commit, author grain-ww, signature N by design, no sshCommand in seed config, IDENT_CLEAN on the standing scan, and the seed's own README carries the crashed-meteor badge. The commit-guard witness is GREEN over the whole rename -- 25 planted cases, the armed pen biting on the new prefix.
obs The phase name earns its image: primordial was the molten field before any face; the crashed meteor is the seed landed in public ground, still hot, the crater the first thing a stranger finds.
obs Mid-round, Keaton created the grain-ww ORGANIZATION and asked for ww as another upstream synonym of seed. gh repo create grain-ww/grain answered with the repo, the publisher gained the second door -- one projection, force-pushed to both origin (grain-os/grain) and ww (grain-ww/grain) -- and the live meteor was pushed to ww at once: both doors read e507f1c. The roster seats ww beside seed as peer names for one seed, never two seeds.
loom seed_before=c06eb0a seed_after=e507f1c leak_caught=seed/.git/config publisher_corrections=2 rule_twins_updated=4 front_door_pages=3 seed_doors=2
